      "notes": "Positive photoresist (5 um, sensitive at 350-400 nm, typical exposure 90 s, developing under 45 s at 20 C) on first-choice FR4 laminate with a UV blocker, with protective foil; boards of 0.5 to 2.5 mm (the 1.5 mm is sold as 1.5 or 1.6) with 18, 35 or 70 um copper (105 um at 1.5 mm); standard cuttings for 1.5 mm with 35 and 70 um copper: 210x300, 200x250, 150x250, 160x233.4, 150x200, 125x175, 100x160 and 75x100 mm; panels 510x1150 and 510x570 mm; pre-sensitizing service up to 530x1160 mm. Two sheets describe the base material and they differ: the IPC 4101A sheet gives Tg 150 C (specification 110-150), Td 320 C, Z CTE 15/250 and X-Y 15/17 ppm/C, thermal conductivity 0.36 W/mK, Dk 4.8/4.6/4.5 and Df 0.015, volume resistivity 4.0e8 MOhm cm and surface 3.0e6 MOhm after moisture resistance (converted to ohm), arc resistance 105 s, CTI 205 V (class 3), flexural strength 442 and 435 (printed GPa; the specification of 415 and 345 is in MPa, so MPa is taken), moisture absorption 0.20 %; the DIN IEC 249 sheet gives Tg 140 +-5 C, Z CTE 5e-5 below and 20e-5 above Tg per C, Dk 4.2-4.8 and Df 0.01-0.016 at 1 MHz, flexural 485-550 and 400-450 N/mm2, moisture absorption below 0.10 %, dielectric breakdown above 60 kV and arc resistance above 120 s. Peel strength printed as 145 N/mm on the IPC sheet is not used (a missing decimal point). Thickness tolerance 1.55 +-0.08 mm, copper 35 +-5 um.",
      "source": {
        "pdf": "katalog_en.pdf",
        "pages": "6-7"
